{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And it shall be that the man whom I shall choose, his staff shall blossom, and I will quiet from upon Me.</b> This verse indicates that they were still complaining after three punishments had been done among them — swallowing, burning, and plague — and therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, needed to make for them the sign of the blossoming of the staff after these three punishments. For the swallowing of Korah and his companions was a sign and wonder that the Holy One, blessed be He, rejected the firstborn — since Korah was a firstborn, as I explained above; and the burning of the incense-offerers was a sign regarding the priesthood, that the Holy One, blessed be He, chose Aaron to be high priest and to offer incense before Him, and therefore the incense-offerers were burned while he alone remained; and for the complaint they made, in that they did not accept the exchange, the punishment of the plague came upon them. And they were still complaining after the plague, as it says: ״והשכתי מעלי את תלונות״ — and I will quiet from upon Me the complaints; and therefore the sign of the blossoming of the staff was needed, to indicate the sprouting of calamity for all who dispute, and it was as a sign of covenant upon the Levites, for the Holy One, blessed be He, chose the Levites in place of the firstborn. And this is what the verse says: לבית לוי — the verse teaches you that the blossoming of the staff was a sign and wonder upon the Levite service." "<b>And behold</b> — through all these signs it has been explained that the prophecy of Moses is true and established, and the words of the disputants who doubt the words of Moses, who say about him that he performed the deeds from his own knowledge, are broken — and then they will know with clarity that all is from before the Holy One, blessed be He."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The phrase 'והשכתי מעלי את תלונות' appears to be R. Bahya's paraphrastic rendering of the verse's sense rather than a verbatim quotation; Numbers 17:20 (17:5 in some numbering) reads 'והשכתי מעליכם את תלונתיכם.' Translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:37.133886226Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}